                                            </msIdentifier>
                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch, for Coptic use, with commentary of Mark ibn Qanbar</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-16-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="3" to="58"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-16-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="59" to="108v"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-16-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="109" to="145v"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-16-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="146v" to="192v"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-16-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="193" to="236"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Text identical to that of MS Arabe 10.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper; ff. 1-4 remade in Western paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_7ea4290671edc6070a6123): Nombreuses gloses marginales et interlinéaires. 19 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 190 × 115 mm. Cahiers numérotés en lettres arabes à 10 fol.Papier oriental (sauf les fol. 1-4 refaits en papier occidental). 239 fol. (f. 146 laissé en blanc). Folioté en chiffres coptes. Écriture orientale (Égypte). — Titres rubriqués. 250 × 170 mm. Reliure orientale à rabat, basane brune. Médaillon et filets estampés à froid.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">239 folios (f. 146 blank); foliated in Coptic numerals</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">250</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">170</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">19 lines per page. Gatherings numbered in Arabic letters, 10 folios per gathering. Numerous marginal and interlinear glosses.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="19" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">190</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">115</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian. Four hands are noted at ff. 1v-2v, 3r-4v, 5r-20v, and 231r-232v.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Rubricated titles.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental binding with flap, brown sheepskin; medallion and fillets stamped cold.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_7ea4290671edc6070a6123): Pentateuque, à l&apos;usage des coptes, avec commentaire de Marc ibn Qanbar. Date described in the BnF catalogue: 1238.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Notice by J. Ascari. Bought in the Orient by de Maillet. Coptic calendar at ff. 1v-2v; mark of Yūsuf ʿAṭiyya at f. 2; anonymous reader marks at ff. 20-20v and f. 58v; reading mark of Yaʿqūb ibn Ǧirǧis dated 13 Abīb 1209 of the Martyrs / 1493 at f. 192v; note on epacts and Coptic ecclesiastical computus at ff. 236v-239; anonymous reader mark dated 1175 of the Martyrs / 1459 at f. 239v.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" when="1238">1238</origDate>
                                                    <p>Four hands are identified at ff. 1v-2v, 3r-4v, 5r-20v, and 231r-232v. The copy of the rest of the volume was completed on 23 Barmahāt 954 of the Martyrs (f. 236).</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
